course: dictionary
lesson: 13967
title: Linguistic: all about language
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Linguistic is a long word, but its meaning is simple. It means to do with language. Language is the words we use to speak, read and write. So a linguistic skill is a skill with words, such as reading well or writing a clear story.
explain: «Her linguistic skills helped her write a clear story.» The clues are write and story, so linguistic skills must be skills with words. Linguistic can also mean to do with linguistics, the science that studies how languages work. A person who studies this is a linguist.
explain: Look for the thing the word describes. «The class studied the linguistic features of the poem, like its rhyme and word choice.» Features are things you can spot in a text, so linguistic features are the language tricks a writer uses. Ask yourself: linguistic of what?
fact: Linguistic means to do with language or languages.
fact: Linguistics is the science that studies how languages work.
fact: «Linguistic diversity» means many different languages in one place, such as a school where children speak many home languages.
fact: «Linguistic puzzles» are word puzzles, like the ones in some language olympiads.
fact: Linguistic is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in «linguistic skills».
exercise: «Her linguistic skills helped her write a clear story.» What does linguistic mean here? | To do with the weather | To do with running fast | To do with cooking | *To do with language
exercise: «The school has great linguistic diversity, with children speaking many home languages.» What does linguistic diversity mean? | A loud noise in the hall | One single language only | *Many different languages | Lots of different sports
exercise: Which word names the science that studies how languages work? | *Linguistics | Astronomy | Biology | Geography
test: «The linguistic features of the text were word choice and short, sharp sentences.» What are linguistic features? | *Language tricks a writer uses | Pictures in the book | The name of the author | The page numbers
test: Which of these is a linguistic puzzle? | *A word puzzle about the meanings of words | A maze drawn on paper | A sudoku of numbers | A jigsaw of a farm
exam: Ayaan says a linguistic puzzle is a puzzle about cars. Is he right? | Yes, it is about cars and engines | *No, it is about language and words | Yes, it is about football | Yes, it is about maths only
